      "side": 1,
      "message": "In the android12-5.10 version of this CL, qperret@ asked a question that didn\u0027t get answered, so I\u0027ll ask again now:\n\n\"Right, this all feels a bit fragile. Where is the flag consumed? In the vendor implementation of select_task_rq_*()? If so, could we simply replace this wake flag by a flag in the VENDOR part of task_struct?\"\n\nWith qperret@\u0027s suggestion, this could be implemented completely from a vendor module and no flag would be needed. Can that work? If not, why not?",
      "revId": "6704227e14e37119c20f5bd3ff1766256e05f448",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "552438c5_c3f83035",
        "filename": "kernel/sched/sched.h",
